# NestJS Server Conventions

Applies to `server/`.

## Feature module checklist

Each feature folder under `server/src/` should include:

- `*.module.ts` — registers controller, service, and imports
- `*.controller.ts` — HTTP routes only
- `*.service.ts` — business logic
- `dto/` — request validation classes
- `entities/` — TypeORM entities (when persisted)
- `interfaces/` — response/API shapes (optional, when not covered by DTOs)

Infrastructure modules (`database/`, `storage/`, `common/`) follow the same naming pattern but may omit controllers or entities.

## Controller rules

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — delegate to service
@Post()
create(@Body() dto: CreateMeetingDto) {
  return this.meetingsService.create(dto);
}

// ❌ BAD — business logic in controller
@Post()
create(@Body() dto: CreateMeetingDto) {
  const meeting = this.repo.create(dto);
  return this.repo.save(meeting);
}
```

## Common code

Place guards, pipes, filters, interceptors, middleware, and decorators in `server/src/common/`, not inside feature modules unless feature-specific.

## Service rules

- One primary responsibility per service.
- Split when handling unrelated domains (e.g. `MeetingsService` vs `BlobStorageService` in `storage/`).
